{"authored" [{"question" "q-334452" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the constant particular solution to the following Clairaut differential equation:\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}+{y}^{′}-3.\n$$" "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-334452/review.json" "file_sha256" "5d98950a4383a30cef8b80b0e9264c4ed8f4bf9b82b9c96716b707daa7cfcfdd" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-334452/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "eb0d2d1f0d504544537d895b534150c55ee21df2b47c9d2deee5e7e5cabacbe1" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-334452/verification.json" "basis" 1806 "rationale" "The source asks for a singular function although its parameter envelope degenerates to the point (-1,-3). The original solver correctly refused a nonexistent singular answer. The explicitly authored constant-particular-solution request has unique y=-3, whose actual submitted source grade is Correct. Correct the study request and complete solution consistently while retaining the source key/choices and existing immutable fields/answers. Preserve original request, source explanation, original false confidence and grade separately."} {"question" "q-334452" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A constant particular solution has $y'=0$. Substituting this into\n\n$$y=xy'+y'-3$$\n\ngives $y=-3$. Its derivative is zero, and direct substitution verifies\n\n$$-3=x\\cdot0+0-3.$$\n\nTherefore, the constant particular solution is $y=-3$.\n\nTo distinguish this from a singular solution, write $p=y'$. The equation becomes $y=(x+1)p-3$, and differentiation gives $0=(x+1)p'$. The ordinary straight-line family is\n\n$$y=c(x+1)-3,$$\n\nwith arbitrary constant $c$. The envelope condition obtained by differentiating this family with respect to $c$ is $x+1=0$. It forces $x=-1$ and $y=-3$, giving a single point rather than a singular graph $y(x)$. The constant solution $y=-3$ is the ordinary family member $c=0$; it is not a separate singular solution." "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-334452/review.json" "file_sha256" "5d98950a4383a30cef8b80b0e9264c4ed8f4bf9b82b9c96716b707daa7cfcfdd" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-334452/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "eb0d2d1f0d504544537d895b534150c55ee21df2b47c9d2deee5e7e5cabacbe1" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-334452/verification.json" "basis" 1806 "rationale" "The source asks for a singular function although its parameter envelope degenerates to the point (-1,-3). The original solver correctly refused a nonexistent singular answer. The explicitly authored constant-particular-solution request has unique y=-3, whose actual submitted source grade is Correct. Correct the study request and complete solution consistently while retaining the source key/choices and existing immutable fields/answers. Preserve original request, source explanation, original false confidence and grade separately."} {"question" "q-334452" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=-3"] "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-334452/review.json" "file_sha256" "5d98950a4383a30cef8b80b0e9264c4ed8f4bf9b82b9c96716b707daa7cfcfdd" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-334452/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "eb0d2d1f0d504544537d895b534150c55ee21df2b47c9d2deee5e7e5cabacbe1" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-334452/verification.json" "basis" 1806 "rationale" "The source asks for a singular function although its parameter envelope degenerates to the point (-1,-3). The original solver correctly refused a nonexistent singular answer. The explicitly authored constant-particular-solution request has unique y=-3, whose actual submitted source grade is Correct. Correct the study request and complete solution consistently while retaining the source key/choices and existing immutable fields/answers. Preserve original request, source explanation, original false confidence and grade separately."} {"question" "q-334452" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the singular solution to the following Clairaut differential equation:\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}+{y}^{′}-3.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054585/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b6f52bf096bc380c09c75f64a43d61f77e8e2f654b76fbf513f0e8a92c05bf0" "basis" 1805 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054585/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-334452" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A Clairaut differential equation has the form\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}+g({y}^{′}),\n$$\n\nwhere $g$ is a differentiable function of ${y}^{′}.$\n\nTo solve the Clairaut differential equation\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}+{y}^{′}-3,\n$$\n\nwe start by setting $p={y}^{′}.$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation gives\n\n$$\ny=xp+p-3.\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =(xp+p-3)^{′} \\\\ p & =p+x{p}^{′}+{p}^{′} \\\\ 0 & ={p}^{′}(x+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe product on the right-hand side equals zero, so at least one factor must be zero.\n\nThe singular solution of the Clairaut differential equation is obtained if $x+1=0.$ Then,\n\n$$\nx=-1.\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute this into $y=xp+p-3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =xp+p-3 \\\\  & =(-1)p+p-3 \\\\  & =-p+p-3 \\\\  & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the explicit form of the singular solution is\n\n$$\ny=-3.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054585/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b6f52bf096bc380c09c75f64a43d61f77e8e2f654b76fbf513f0e8a92c05bf0" "basis" 1805 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054585/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-334452" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054585/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b0740448e9b720813dc79f7eb466eb59030d4da806e29825ec90a5d160413409" "basis" 1805 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054585/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-334452" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054585/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b6f52bf096bc380c09c75f64a43d61f77e8e2f654b76fbf513f0e8a92c05bf0" "basis" 1805 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054585/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-334452" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=-3"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054585/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b6f52bf096bc380c09c75f64a43d61f77e8e2f654b76fbf513f0e8a92c05bf0" "basis" 1805 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differen